{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfkziz5YEtbeGNtaw4e27","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote the candidate, and the self-check passed (`OK`). The smoke fit took about 15 minutes, which is half of admission's 30-minute limit per sampling run, so speed could be tight.\n\n**Model:** `diminishing_switch_impression_dilution`, a refinement of the incumbent `short_sequence_pseudoflip_dilution`.\n\n**Why:** The one critique that survives FDR is that in long pairs (6+ flips) where both sequences have at most two switches, people pick the more-switching sequence more often than the incumbent predicts (0.872 observed vs 0.839 predicted, q = 0.048). In other words, the first one or two breaks of a streak count for more than the model allows.\n\n**The change:** In the incumbent, a person's impression of how often a sequence switches grows in a straight line with the number of switches. In my version it grows with diminishing returns, along a fitted curve `((k+1)^ρ − 1)/ρ`, where k is the number of switches. At ρ = 1 this is exactly the incumbent's straight line. Below 1, the first breaks in a streak make a sequence look much more random and each further switch adds less. That is one new parameter, `log_rho`, with a Normal(0, 0.5) prior. Everything else is unchanged.\n\n**Self-check results:**\n- The model loads, its log-probability is finite and it meets the data contract.\n- The smoke fit gave an ELPD-LOO of −3563.4. That is a single 100-draw chain, so it isn't comparable to the incumbent's full-fit −3566.8 and doesn't show the new model is better.\n- Two warnings: convergence wasn't checked (R-hat needs more than one chain), and PSIS-LOO came out unreliable on this short fit (6.6% of trials have Pareto k above 0.5, against a 1% tolerance). Admission's full fit will decide both.\n\nThe novelty check against the live models wasn't run. If ρ is fitted close to 1, the predictions may be too close to the incumbent's and the gate would reject it.\n\nThe incumbent's linear switch-difference input is still in `prepare_observed`, but the model no longer uses it.\n\nFiles are in `experiment3/model_loop/iter_3/candidate_3/`:\n- `hypothesis.md`\n- `model_name.txt`\n- `candidate.py`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":86792,"cache_read_input_tokens":11602,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":86792,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d9d8863f-1ac2-40a5-bb29-5b075bead48f","uuid":"4d0eff33-a8e6-4b9c-bc0b-baf87be1815e","timestamp":"2026-10-06T12:38:07.614Z","request_id":"req_011CfkziyfyAHUjavGrHXhSi"}
